Hi everybody,

Some time ago, I sent out a question concerniog rev. G of QLA1040
SCSI adapter being not recognized by console firmware in au-series
DPWs. It is recognized, but not initialized due to the lack of
firmware by DU 4.0d. At the same time, the Digital KZPBA (which
in our case appears to be an unmodified[*] rev E. of QLA1040)
works fine.

I got no useful replies to that request, which lead me to investigate
a bit further. Disassembling the DU's Qlogic ISP driver (which is in
/sys/BINARY/isp.mod) reveals that it contains the code to reload
firmware of the Qlogic 1020/1040 adapters[**]. The firmware itself is
supposed to be in /dev/qlogic/isp_fw.mod. Unfortunately, my skill at reading
