this file is supposed to be[+]. Placing binary image of the firmware[++] 
in /dev/qlogic/isp_fw.mod does not work - the driver attempts to get
the firmware, but aborts with: "Unsupported firmware image file format".
(The message appears to come from the driver's routine responsible 
for loading firmware image into memory. It does not attempt to download
it to the card itself).

This brings me to yet another question: does anybody here know that
the format of /dev/qlogic/isp_fw.mod is supposed to be, or better
still can share his/her copy of it with us?

Thanks for your attention,

/Serge.P


[*] That's according our DEC sales rep.

[**] Which means that you still can't boot from it. That's fine 
for us - we want to use this card alongside the KZPBA.

[+] Naturally (well, for Digital), the format (or existence) of
/dev/qlogic/isp_fw.mod does not appear to be documented anywhere.
I also can't find any trace of it by grepping through the entire
contents of our Firmware and DU 4.0d CDs.

[++] included with the Linux-Alpha ISP driver, and also easy to
extract from the QLOGIC's x86 boot PROM on the card itself.

