From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Aug 27 17:15:34 1998
From: Steve Wilson <Steve.Wilson () itron ! com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 1998 17:15:34 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY:  Re: DU 4.0b downgrade
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078718211996

The DU 4.0b OS is correct in its system assessment. The 4.0b Unix does not
have native support for the latest cards shipped with the Alpha 1000A's. A
response from Oisin McGuinness summarizes the problem:

The likely problem is you have a DE500-BA card; support for that is in
4.0D, or
in patch kit 6 or higher for 4.0B.

Thanks to all who responded.

Steve Wilson



