directly from Digital. As with most projects where you want
to save some money, we'd run into some trouble.

The Digital's KZPBA card we have in our DPW and QLA1040 look 
essentially identical. The only differences are:

                      KZPBA            QLA1040

Card rev:       PC2010403-11-E     PC2010403-09-G
ISP1040 batch:  MCL7E01/N9728D     MIPL64/N9816D

The ISP1040 part numbers are the same on both cards.

Now the trouble begins: if I put the QLA card in the
third 32-bit PCI slot of DPW (first two slots are 
occupied by the graphics card and KZPBA), the card is
not recognized by the console firmware, so that nothing
shows up under "show dev". "show config" actually lists
the PCI slot 10 as occupied, with unknown card having
vendor id 1077 (Qlogic) and device id 1020 (QLA 10[24]*
series). Taking the KZPBA out and putting QLA1040 in the
second PCI slot does not make any difference - it is
still not recognized.

If I try to boot genvmunix at this point, it recognizes
the QLA card as an ISP-based SCSI controller (no surprise, 
since it is listed in /etc/sysconfigtab), but refuses to 
work with is due to missing on-board firmware (which 
should have been loaded by the console?):

Aug 24 10:29:03 cobalt24 vmunix: isp1 at pci1000 slot 10
Aug 24 10:29:03 cobalt24 vmunix: cam_logger: CAM_ERROR packet
Aug 24 10:29:03 cobalt24 vmunix: cam_logger: bus 3
