does anybody know what this means
is my network card knackered??
 Aug 18 12:11:20 noreen vmunix: NFS2 server noreen.apion-ti.com ok
 Aug 18 12:19:38 noreen vmunix: tu1: transmit FIFO underflow: threshold
raised to: 256 bytes
 Aug 18 12:26:10 noreen vmunix: tu1: transmit FIFO underflow: threshold
raised to: 512 bytes
{reply}
This is normal.  The tulip device driver will step down the network card
when it detects an error.  On our network our tulip cards, DE500, step
down to 256, 512, 1024 bytes, and then finally store-forward due to our
busy network interface.
If you execute 'netstat -i', you will note at least 2 errors -- once for
each threshold change.

