=09
/sbin/vdump is part of the OSFADVFS subset.  Are you using AdvFS?  Did you
install the AdvFS subset?  If not, go back to the distribution CDROM and
install AdvFS BasePolyCenter AdvFS (System Administration).  You really
only need vdump if you are processing AdvFS filesystems.  If yoou do not
use AdvFS then you can run /sbin/dump and /sbin/restore for backups and
recoveries.

