   Nestor Ruiz
   Ian Goodacre

   My problem was that root�s account was disabled because of many
unsuccesful logins.

   The problem was solved going single user and using edauth to make
the following changes in root�s authentication database:

    - remove u_numunsuclog
    - setting u_maxtries to u_maxtries#0

   It was also suggested to check that the field ulock@ exists.

