alpha 2100A ver 4.0B kzpsc-ba 

Question : 
	Firstly , I have a 2100A with two swxcr controllers ,
I want to add a third one . Is this possible or is there a limit .
Seondly , I want to move the existing swxcr controllers
and a scsi controller to other  PCI slots , can I do this if
I boot from genvmunix and run sizer etc. and build a new kernel .
I do not want to have to restore the disks on the two
existing controllers .

Thanks to : Alan Rollow, Michael A Crowley, Mervyn Weis 

Answer : 
	The limit is 4 on a 2100A
	If you install swxcr controllers , install them up top of the
	the slots with free ones below . The system scans from
	top to bottom and allocates names eg: re0 to the first
	controller it finds . My two controllers were at the bottom.
	I moved my contollers up and installed the new one below them . 
	I then ran sizer -n FOO and installed the new lines in my
	conf file and built a new kernel .
 
controller      xcr0       at pci0      slot  7 vector    xcrintr
                             -----           ---
controller      xcr0       at pci2000   slot  9 vector    xcrintr
			      -------        ---
	There are two PCI buses . The primary (0) is the bottom 4 slots.
	The secondary (2) is the top four . 
		
	Gotchas : The vga card seems like it has to be at the
	very bottom slot . Moving it causes dummyspits . 
	When I used swxcrmgr to configure my new controller
	I noticed that the new one was contoller 2 and my two old
	ones where controllers 1 and 3 . ( Had been 1 & 2 )
	I was very nearly caught out by presuming the new controller
	would be 3 and went to create a new config on it .
	P.S. All my data remained intact . 


