Hi DU Admins

My question was about this warning message seen at powerup on our 
PW 500au and 433au series workstations.

Thanks to Peter Stern, Graham Allan for their replies and to
Richard Bemrose for supplying all the information he had on this 
problem.

The solution for us came from Nick Sayer of Digital Support in 
Brisbane who advised me to upgrade to firmware version 5.2. I 
downloaded the firmware from Digital's site, installed it from 
a floppy and the error message is gone.  

Whether this really fixes anything or just eliminates the warning 
message remains to be seen.

More details of the firmware that fixed the problem:

   >>> sho conf

   SRM Console:  V6.8-41
   ARC Console:  5.65
   PALCode:      VMS PALcode V1.20-14,  OSF PALcode V1.22-17
   SROM version: V5.90

More details of the replies and other information I was able
to gather:

Opinions differ on whether this is a real problem or not
and the suggested possible solutions range over:

   upgrading the firmware
   replacing the motherboard
   replacing a disk
   replacing the Bcache module
   installing a Bcache module if there is none installed

Some of our workstations have Bcache and some don't, and adding a 
Bcache module to one didn't eliminate the message so I didn't believe
the cache was relevant.  

Some have one disk and some two and the disk models are different so
I doubted the disks had anything to do with it.

Replacing the motherboard seemed like a last resort so I tried
the firmware upgrade and it worked.


Ian

